WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.680
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.140
Now let’s have a look at how you can upload

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.800
your pre-recorded videos to your YouTube channel.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.140
Let’s go!

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.980
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.740
On YouTube, you will always see this

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.140
PLUS button around the top right region.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.040
When you click on it,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.820
you will be given two options.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.560
To upload a video; or to go live!

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.540
In this video, we will only concentrate on

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.680
how to upload videos.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.940
So, click on the Upload video link

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.040
which will bring you to this screen!

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.220
YouTube is now asking you to select

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.320
The video files that you want to upload.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.620
And yes, you can upload more than

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.940
one video at once.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.100
Let’s try uploading a video now!

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.620
You can click on the Select Files button,

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.600
select the video you wish to upload, and then

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.580
click on Open.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.840
The uploading process has now begun,

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.340
and you will see the name of the

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:56.480
video file you uploaded here!

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.520
The progress bar at the bottom tells you what

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.900
percentage of your video has been uploaded.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.640
After the video is uploaded, YouTube will

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:05.400
take a few seconds to process it,

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:06.560
and then you will see

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.680
the ‘Finished Processing’ sign.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:09.880
At this point, you’re ready to

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.240
add the details about your video.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.160
The first step is to add a title and

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.060
a description of your video.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.320
They should both be short, crisp

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.500
and must also include important keywords.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.360
Having good titles and descriptions will

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.220
not only help your viewers but will also help

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.680
you with Google search rankings,

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.720
more watch time, and more subscribers.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.080
Yes, good titles and descriptions will

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.780
help your channel grow significantly.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.560
The top part should always contain

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.820
the actual description of your video.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.680
And then you could add your school website link,

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.220
or your youtube channel subscription

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.580
link, and so on.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.620
So the description box is not just about

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.040
the description of your video, but a lot more.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.780
Another important aspect of the video that

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.800
many people overlook on YouTube

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.360
is the ‘Custom Thumbnail’ option.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.320
What’s a thumbnail?

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.040
A thumbnail is an image you upload along with your that helps your viewers understand

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.280
what your video is all about, with a
glance.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.680
You can also call it a marketing image for your video.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.500
You will get to upload a custom thumbnail

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.300
only after your account is verified in good standing.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.700
We will see how to do that in the upcoming videos.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.580
You are also expected to

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.120
truthfully answer these questions here.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.980
If your content is made for kids,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.020
then you need to select this option.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.380
This helps YouTube

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.920
create a safer environment for children.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.280
If your content is not made for kids,

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:37.080
select the 2nd option here, and here as well.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.180
You should know that YouTube has specific definitions

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.240
for the term “Made for Kids”

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.820
To know more about it,

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:45.820
check out the link in the description below.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.020
Let’s mark it as ‘Made for kids’ here.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.760
You can also click on ‘More Options’

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.500
and fill in more details about your video.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.180
You should especially focus on the Tags section.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.400
Add all the important

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.660
tag words related to your video.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.000
These tags could be something

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.600
that many students search for.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.640
You could also then select the Education category here.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.780
So what next?

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.440
Clicking on ‘Next’ will lead you to the

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.040
Video Elements page.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.540
These are additional overlays you can use

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.880
on your video to lead your viewers to your other videos.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.720
And then we come to the last stage of Visibility

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.700
which gives you four options.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.240
If you keep it public, then anybody who visits YouTube

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:30.800
could watch your video.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.280
If your video is unlisted, then only people

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.200
with your video, link will be able to watch

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.260
your video and nobody will be able to find

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:40.540
it just by searching on youtube.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.300
And if you keep it private, then you could share

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.940
it with specific people only by adding their Gmail IDs.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.980
To understand this better, take a moment

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.960
to pause this video, and check out this table.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.420
But many times, we don’t want to publish

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.680
the videos immediately.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.980
So YouTube also gives us this option to

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.620
SCHEDULE our video.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.020
For now, let’s keep it public.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.880
With this, your video is now uploaded,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.880
and ready to reach the world.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.780
You could also then go to the My channel option on the

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:12.820
top right corner, and you will see

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:15.320
a video under the Videos tab here.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.500
So now you know how you can upload your videos to

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.740
your YouTube channel.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:23.420
The next session will be very interesting!

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:26.860
I will talk about how you can go LIVE on YouTube!

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:27.800
See you there.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:35.560
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.700
[ YouTube Learning ]

